        "quiz_type": "single_choice",
        "question_type": "single_choice",
        "question_title": "A triangle \\(ABC\\) is to be constructed with \\(BC=a\\), \\(AB+AC=s\\), and \\(\\angle ABC=\\beta\\). Which construction is valid, assuming a solution exists?",
        "question_instruction": "Choose one correct option.",
        "explanation": "Choose \\(D\\) on the ray from \\(B\\) making angle \\(\\beta\\) with \\(BC\\), with \\(BD=s\\). If \\(A\\) lies on the perpendicular bisector of \\(CD\\), then \\(AD=AC\\). Since \\(A\\) lies between \\(B\\) and \\(D\\), \\(BD=BA+AD=AB+AC=s\\).",
        "question_audio": null,
        "time_limit_seconds": 30,
        "points": 10,
        "sort_order": 123,
        "question_data": {
          "_meta": {
