        "question_title": "Let a circle with centre \\(O\\) and radius \\(r\\) be given, and let \\(P\\) be an exterior point. Which is the standard construction for the tangents from \\(P\\) to the circle?",
        "question_instruction": "Choose one correct option.",
        "explanation": "If \\(T\\) lies on the circle with diameter \\(OP\\), then \\(\\angle OTP=90^\\\\circ\\). Therefore \\(PT\\perp OT\\), making \\(PT\\) a tangent to the given circle.",
